 "prose": [
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "← Unfold"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Realizations & carriers"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "tab-carriers",
   "text": "Carriers"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "tab-extensions",
   "text": "Build a map"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "tab-solids",
   "text": "Prisms & cones"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Complex"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "placement",
   "text": "Change drawing"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Δ lists the faces. |Δ| contains every point of the corresponding filled simplices."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Abstract complex Δ"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Vertices"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "{a}"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "{b}"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Edges"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Select a face σ."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A drawing of |Δ|"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": "real-caption",
   "text": "σ = {a,b}. Its realization contains the whole segment, not just its endpoints."
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "λa0.50"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "λb0.50"
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "What exactly is being realized?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "A face σ is a finite set of vertex names. Its geometric simplex ⟨σ⟩ contains all convex combinations of those vertices: λᵢ ≥ 0 and ∑λᵢ = 1. The realization |Δ| is the union of these simplices."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "In the standard realization, each vertex is a basis vector eᵥ. Thus a point is the coordinate vector (λₐ, λᵦ, …). Only mixtures whose positive-coordinate support is a face of Δ belong to |Δ|. The planar drawing uses other vertex positions and the same weights."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Moving vertices in a valid drawing preserves the abstract complex. Adding a filled triangle changes the complex. The empty face contributes no points."
  }
 ],
